eople  um and it just goes to say about the  source material how wonderful it is  i feel like this has just been aching  like you know people have been aching  for it for like 30 years like it's so  striking and unique the the comic book  so to finally get that  brought to live action i feel like it's  more you know instead of the  instead of the kind of nervousness and  anticipation like i personally feel  coming in and sneaking around the sets  and looking at the production design and  seeing what can  you know creatively it's such a unique  world so getting to to see that come to  life i kind of just feel  buzzed and like thrilled and excited  yeah i mean we can only  [Music]  the the creative team behind this was  really great and you know everyone put  their hearts into this and so many  people you know on the production team  were fans of it and we can only hope  that we did a good job  and i think that because neil is just  part of every aspect of this he's all  over it it's still his voice it's still  what he wanted it to be so that for me  as an actor anyway it made me feel  really secure  in what i was doing in the world that we  were creating and you've got allen's  incredible script so it's like you just  exciting  a bit of pressure but super exciting  yeah so i don't want to do any spoilers  as i asked the other group i'm going to  ask you the same question you guys have  10 episodes in the first season  which of the 10 was your favorite or  which of the 10 are you most looking  forward to the audience seeing  i think the buzz around town is episode  5 is quite good  however i'm not in that  so it's not  episode 9 for me was um just a  treat of how they actually pulled off  the convention  and the type of characters that were  there  if that's  just enough  episode 9 is great  um i'm most anticipating eight and nine  um  just simply the same as boyd said just  you know seeing all of the fantastical  things that happen at the convention  um i'd genuinely